          position: 3,
          name: "Blacktop Sealer Cost",
          item: "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/blacktop-sealer-cost/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does blacktop sealer cost per gallon or bucket?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Blacktop sealer costs $5–$6 per gallon ($25–$30 per 5-gallon bucket) for economy asphalt emulsion, $7–$9 per gallon ($35–$45 per bucket) for mid-range polymer-modified emulsion, and $11–$14 per gallon ($55–$70 per bucket) for premium coal tar or heavy-duty formulas. Price per gallon isn't the whole story — coverage rate varies by tier, so a cheaper bucket that covers less area can end up costing more per square foot than a pricier one that covers more.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does blacktop sealer cost to seal an entire driveway?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For a one-car driveway (about 250 sq ft), expect to spend $25–$70 on sealer alone depending on tier. A standard two-car driveway (about 500 sq ft) runs $50–$140 in materials. A large driveway (around 1,000 sq ft) costs $75–$280. These figures cover the sealer only — budget separately for crack filler, degreaser, and applicator tools, which typically add another $40–$100.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is more expensive blacktop sealer worth the extra cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually yes, but the margin is thinner than the sticker price suggests. On a cost-per-year-of-protection basis, economy asphalt emulsion runs about $17–$30 per year, mid-range polymer-modified emulsion runs $18–$30 per year, and premium coal tar runs $22–$35 per year — coal tar's longer service life mostly offsets its higher upfront price rather than delivering dramatically cheaper long-term ownership. Premium sealer earns its cost primarily through better chemical resistance to gas and oil spills and a thicker, more durable film, not through lower annual cost.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Why do coal tar sealers cost more than asphalt emulsion sealers?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Coal tar sealers cost more because the raw material itself is pricier than asphalt emulsion, the manufacturing process requires more careful handling due to fumes and PAH content, and coal tar delivers superior chemical resistance that commands a premium in the marketplace. You're also paying for a longer reseal interval — 4–5 years versus 2–3 years for standard emulsion — which is baked into the higher per-bucket price. Coal tar sealers are also banned in several states and municipalities, including Washington and Minnesota, so limited availability affects price in some regions too.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the cost of blacktop sealer include labor?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "No. Every price in this guide is for materials only — the sealer product itself, not application labor. If you hire a professional, labor typically adds $0.10–$0.50 per square foot on top of materials, pushing a two-car driveway project to $125–$450 installed. DIY application avoids that labor cost entirely; a standard two-car driveway takes about 2–4 hours to apply yourself. For the complete cost breakdown including labor, tools, and regional pricing, see our full guide to how much it costs to seal a driveway.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(),
      datePublished: "2026-08-06",
      dateModified: "2026-08-06",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
      description: description,
      mainEntityOfPage: {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": "https://www.thehonestreviewers.com/blacktop-sealer-cost/",
      },
    },
  ],
};
